{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_1eb39b9821f70a66ecf6d83d3f738c1c9f262db3f585b309cf74bae47aa2cba6", "title": "Euroinvestor", "text": "Euroinvestor.com A/S is a Danish media company, operating the financial news and information website Euroinvestor as well as several additional websites and subsidiaries. Established by Søren and Jens Almindes in 1997, the company is currently majority owned by Saxo Bank, having acquired a majority stake in April 2011.", "score": 32.2223}, {"id": "hp_doc_4f47ebbd24db7f402cc8adb1f727509e36ff878efef108d88e569989a8994c46", "title": "Amsprop", "text": "Amsprop is the property company of Alan Sugar. Amsprop now holds the majority of Sugar's £800 million wealth and owns several office building freeholds in Mayfair and other parts of London. Amsprop also owns the Sampson House building on the South Bank of the Thames, which is currently leased back to IBM.", "score": 27.4397}, {"id": "hp_doc_505b1ca3a41c1d09738e4ded4a1160d8a29bda792f45dd010824d51d64fb56b9", "title": "Bank of Hawaii", "text": "The Bank of Hawaii Corporation (BOH) is a regional commercial bank headquartered in Honolulu, Hawaii. It is Hawaii's second oldest bank and its largest locally owned bank in that the majority of the voting stockholders reside within the state. Bank of Hawaii has the most accounts, customers, branches, and ATMs of any financial institution in the state (although BancWest's First Hawaiian Bank holds a greater number of dollars in deposits). The bank consists of four business segments: retail banking, commercial banking, investment services, and treasury. The bank is currently headed by Chairman, President and Chief Executive Officer, Peter S. Ho.", "score": 17.7127}], "remaining_searches": 2}
